From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] system: gate handoff and snapshot clock adaptations

Require handoff for added x86/ARM migration conversions and ARM/GIC snapshot
subsections. Preserve upstream TSS and cpreg-validation paths otherwise.
Require RR for cross-icount clock and PMCEID adaptations and load-time timer
deferral/stall handling, leaving stock expired-timer RR scheduling unchanged.
Require analysis (which fuzz implies) for the snapshot tick-clamp rewind:
panda_fast_restore and repeated loadvm need it without fuzz.

This bounded gate does not restore whole-engine vanilla parity. RISC-V version11
acceptance needs an early descriptor-selection/version-validation solution and
is deliberately not approximated with post_load rejection here.

